-- Control Group Consortium | Milestone 2 | Enhanced seed
-- Source: the supplied seed.sql, enhanced on 2026-11-17.
-- All people, institutions, activities, prices and costs are fictional.
-- No external dataset was imported. Operational activity: January-June 2026.
-- Timestamps are UTC. Money is USD cents. Dates use YYYY-MM-DD.
-- Load once into an empty schema; fixed IDs intentionally reject a second load.
-- sqlite3 -bail consortium.db ".read create.sql" ".read seed.sql"
-- WARNING: create.sql resets consortium tables. Use a new/disposable database.
--
-- Added depth without a bulk-volume expansion:
--   * varied session starts/durations and non-uniform decision waiting times;
--   * valid concurrent room use on distinct instruments (capacity two);
--   * confocal failure/whole-suite closure -> old slot retained -> later session;
--   * staff absence -> replaced assignment retained -> actual work on replacement;
--   * reconfiguration/cleaning, phased specialist assistance and staff instrument use;
--   * cross-project cost sharing and individual researcher payment responsibility;
--   * prospective three-source rules, exact-cent splits, credits/waiver/surcharge;
--   * expired, renewed, revoked and pending-qualification access cases.
-- Initial quotes are retained; final charges reflect actual usage/billable shares.
-- Request start/end values are acceptable scheduling windows; requested minutes
-- are operating time within them. Minute-only EstimatedUsage descriptions match
-- RequestedDurationMinutes, while other descriptive resource estimates may vary.
-- Runtime writes to a real system must preserve finalized history; this file is
-- a synthetic fixture, not a migration that rewrites an existing live database.
-- Q1 reports logged facility usage hours, not a room-occupancy percentage.
-- Q4 rolls up work segments before comparing assignments. Q5 books adjustments
-- in their authorization month, not in the original charge's month.
--
-- Story anchors: repair EventId=47 and rescheduled EventId=37;
-- personnel replacement EventId=43 and EventId=68;
-- event 45 has additional specialist assistance.

